    },
    {
      "id": "1440",
      "width": 1440,
      "height": 900,
      "input": "mouse"
    }
  ],
  "scrollbars": "touch: hidden (--hide-scrollbars) · mouse: native",
  "browser": {
    "args": [
      "--disable-gpu",
      "--disable-gpu-rasterization",
      "--disable-partial-raster",
      "--disable-skia-runtime-opts",
      "--force-color-profile=srgb",
      "--disable-lcd-text"
    ],
    "why": "Without these, same-HEAD runs differed by 1-40 px (anti-aliasing of rounded corners and focus rings in dialogs); measured 2026-09-24.",
    "inputArgs": {
      "touch": [
        "--blink-settings=primaryPointerType=2,availablePointerTypes=2,primaryHoverType=1,availableHoverTypes=1",
        "--touch-events=enabled",
        "--hide-scrollbars"
      ],
      "mouse": [
        "--blink-settings=primaryPointerType=4,availablePointerTypes=4,primaryHoverType=2,availableHoverTypes=2"
      ]
    },
    "inputWhy": "Input mode is fixed when the browser launches: capture.py writes one launch wrapper per input (browser.args + inputArgs + the Chrome binary) and passes it as the executable. blink-settings pointer 2 = coarse, 4 = fine; hover 1 = none, 2 = hover. The state check compares (pointer: coarse), (hover: hover), innerWidth and innerHeight with the viewport and stops with 78 on a mismatch."
  },
  "notes": [
    "30 scene names are inherited from dev-package/reports/design-consistency/20260912/full/scenes.json; account-admin, password-change, gnb-more are new.",
    "account flags are passed as query (upload/labSettings/operator = 1|0). audit-upload.html ignores them: its account is fixed in audit-upload.tsx (upload on, no GNB).",
    "actions: click(selector) | wait(ms) | waitFor(selector) | select([selector, value]) | pickFile({selector, name, bytes}) | scrollIntoView(selector) | waitImage(selector: complete and naturalWidth > 0) | stable(selector: box, zoom scale and document height unchanged for 150 ms x 3). click first scrolls a target that is outside the window or cut by a scroll container.",
    "gnb-more uses viewports 390 · 844x390 · 820 only: .gnb-more is visible at <= 900px.",
    "primitives (P5 · spec S-DESIGN-STRUCTURE-P5-20260924) is the primitive gallery: static markup of primitives.css classes only, no GNB (STANDALONE in audit-design.tsx), no product components.",
    "upload-register-ok (spec S-DESIGN-FIX-FOLLOWUPS-20260925 Q4) is audit-upload.html?register=ok: register/attach succeed locally and the modal is opened by the real parents UploadEntry and GridAttachEntry (useUploadModalPresence). Without the query audit-upload.html is unchanged.",
    "viewports (spec S-DEVICE-WIDTH-INPUT-20260926 L0a · schema 2): a scene lists viewport ids in `viewports`; without it the scene uses all 6. Capture file = <scene>-<theme>-<viewport id>.png.",
    "require (spec S-DEVICE-WIDTH-INPUT-20260926 L0b): preconditions checked after settling, before metrics and screenshot — {imageLoaded|box|exists: selector}. A false precondition stops the run with 78.",
    "mask (L0b · orchestrator decision, spec gap): selectors hidden with visibility: hidden (box kept) in every capture of the scene — injected with the freeze CSS before actions, checked after settling (each selector must match and hide ≥ 1 element, else 78). Only detail-preview-map · detail-preview-map-value declare it: [data-testid=dt-preview-total] (the measured elapsed time 「총 0.0초」 / 「총 0.1초」 changes from run to run). Not a 부록 B target; metrics are unchanged.",
    "detail-preview-map · detail-preview-map-value · upload-preview-expand (L0b): the real dataset detail page with the fixture preview source (src/components/datasetpreview/fixture.ts) and the upload preview panel alone (src/components/upload/fixture.ts); image = frontend/audit-map.png. upload-preview-expand enters by audit-design.html, so the upload scene lock (audit-upload.html · 4 names · empty query) does not see it. The value scene clicks the map viewport centre with a real pointer (a covering tool receives it) and waits for the value panel to settle; before the layout fix the panel keeps the guide sentence (V4)."
  ],
